      <div type="clause" n="19.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 19.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19.3" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="60" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif sweordhwita oðres monnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.21"/> wæpn to feormunge onfó<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.22"/>, oððe smið monnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.23"/> andweorc, hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.9"/> hit gesund begen agifan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.24"/>, swa hit hwæðer hiora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.25"/> ǽr onfenge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.26"/>, buton hiora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.25"/> hwæðer ǽr þingode, þæt he hit angylde healdan ne ðorfte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19.3" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="60" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif sweordhwita oþres monnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.1"/> wæpn to feormunge onfó, oððe smið monnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.1"/> ondweorc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.9-2"/>, hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.1"/> hit gesund begen agifen, swa hit heora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.10"/> hwæðer ær onfenge, buton heora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.10"/> hweðer ær ðingode, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hit angylde healdan ne þorfte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19.3" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="60" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf sweordhwíta oðres mannes wepen to feormung<hi rend="italic">e</hi> underfó, oððe smið mannes andweorc, hi hit g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>sund begen agyfen, swa hit hwæðer heora ær underfenge, buton heora hweðer ǽr ðingode, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hit angylde healdan ne þorfte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="19.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="61" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis forbator<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.19"/> alicuius arma susceperit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.20"/> ad purgandum, uel faber alicuius opus faciendum, ipsi hoc quietum reddant sicut exceperunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.21-2"/>, nisi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.22-2"/> aliquis eorum ante composuit, cur hoc angilde seruare non<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.19"/> debeant.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.oe.23-2"/> | si non eorum custodiam diffinitis prelocutionibus abdicarant.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="74" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif sweordhwita oðres monnes wæpn to feormunge onfó<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_19-3.attnote.fn.1"/>, oððe smið monnes andweorc, hie hit gesund begen agifan, swa hit hwæðer hiora ǽr onfenge<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_19-3.attnote.fn.2"/>, buton hiora hwæðer ǽr þingode, þæt he hit angylde healdan ne ðorfte.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="23" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="314" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif sweordhwita oðres monnes wæpn to feormunge onfó, oððe smið monnes andweorc, hie hit gesund begen agifan, swa hit hwæðer hiora ǽr onfenge, buton hiora hwæðer ǽr þingode, þæt he hit angylde healdan ne ðorfte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="61" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn ein Schwertfeger<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.de.1"/> eines anderen Mannes Waffe zur Reinigung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.de.2"/> empfängt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.de.3"/> oder ein Schmid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.de.4"/> jemandes Werkzeug<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.de.5"/>, sollen sie beide<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.de.6"/> es unbefleckt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.de.7"/> [von Blutschuld] zurückliefern, wie es jeder von ihnen zuvor empfangen hat: es sei denn, jeder von ihnen hätte zuvor [mit dem Eigenthümer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.de.8"/>] ausbedungen, dass<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.de.9"/> er es [nur] ohne Ersatzpflicht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_19-3.lnote.de.10"/> [für etwa befleckte Waffe] zu bewahren brauchte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a sword-polisher receives another man’s weapon for cleaning, or a smith a person’s tool, let them both give it back unstained [by blood-guilt], as each of them received it before: unless either of them had stipulated before [with the owner] that he need keep it [only] without liability for compensation [for a weapon that might be stained].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="75" ed="#attenborough"/>If a sword-furbisher receives a weapon or a smith receives a tool belonging to another man in order to refurbish it, in either case the article shall be returned in as good condition as that in which it has been received<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_19-3.attnote.n.1"/>, unless it has been stipulated that there shall be no liability on the part of the said furbisher for damage done to it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="413" ed="#whitelock"/>If a sword-polisher receives another man’s weapon to polish it, or a smith a man’s tool, they both are to give it back unstained,<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_19-3.whinote.n.2"/> just as either of them had received it; unless either of them had stipulated that he need not be liable to compensation for it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="315" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a sword-polisher takes another person’s weapon to [re]furbish, or a smith someone’s tool, they must both give it back unhurt just as they received it earlier, unless the two of them earlier agreed, that he [the craftsman] might not be held [liable] for compensation for it.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">man. wæpne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">man. wæpne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">underfó <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">underfó Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">man. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">man. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hi <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hi So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">agyfen <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">agyfen So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">heora <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">heora So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">underfenge <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">underfenge Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">erstes</hi> o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">first o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur,</hi> o <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure, o written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">excipiat</hi> <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">excipiat</hi> Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.21-2" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">recep. <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">recep. Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.22-2" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> nisi — deb. <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> si non — abdic. <hi rend="italic">übrige und Hn</hi> 87, 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only nisi — deb. Lond; only si non — abdic. the others and Hn 87, 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.oe.23-2" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt c.</hi> 16. 17 <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">c. 16. 17 follow in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">politor uel emundator</hi> Hn 87, 3; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Schwert 7</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">politor uel emundator</hi> Hn 87, 3; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Schwert 7</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Herrichtung’ Schmid; doch bed. das Wort ‘Rostiges polieren’; <hi rend="italic">s.</hi> Toller <hi rend="italic">s. v. feormendleas, feormynd</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘preparation’ Schmid; but the word means ‘polishing what is rusty’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Toller <hi rend="italic">s. v. feormendleas, feormynd</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B modernisiert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B modernises</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Metallhandwerker’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘metal-craftsman’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Arbeitsstoff’ (Schmid) kann das Wort zwar bedeuten, passt aber hier nicht. Nur aus md. <hi rend="italic">antwerc,</hi> Fries. <hi rend="italic">onderk</hi> folgt die Bed. ‘Werkzeug’ (auch Brunner II 558); das Wort ist erst später mit ‘Hand’ verwirrt. — Q scheint <hi rend="italic">on weorc</hi> ‘zum Werk’ zu verstehen.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The word can indeed mean ‘working material’ (Schmid), but that does not fit here. The meaning ‘tool’ follows only from Middle German <hi rend="italic">antwerc,</hi> Fris. <hi rend="italic">onderk</hi> (also Brunner II 558); the word was confused with ‘hand’ only later. — Q seems to understand <hi rend="italic">on weorc</hi> ‘for the work’.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘beides’; Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> I 305</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘both things’; Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> I 305</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">quietus</hi> häufiges Juristenlatein in Q = <hi rend="italic">absolutus</hi> in Hn</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">quietus</hi>, frequent legal Latin in Q, = <hi rend="italic">absolutus</hi> in Hn</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Haftung 4e; Anvertrautes 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Haftung 4e; Anvertrautes 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.de.9" n="9" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">cur</hi> ist Q’s eigentümliches Latein. — Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> verstand <hi rend="italic">angilde</hi> nicht; in <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi> soll <hi rend="italic">custodia</hi> vielleicht ‘Haftpflicht’ bedeuten</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">cur</hi> is Q’s idiosyncratic Latin. — Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> did not understand <hi rend="italic">angilde</hi>; in <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi> <hi rend="italic">custodia</hi> is perhaps meant to signify ‘liability’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19-3.lnote.de.10" n="10" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht <hi rend="italic">an gylde</hi> ‘auf Ersatz’; noch auch ‘for a requital’ nach <hi rend="italic">mercedem pro custodia consecutus</hi> (Lex Baiuw. XV 1). Meine Übs. verbindet das dem Instrum. entnommene ‘mit, unter’ und die Negation zu ‘nur ohne’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not <hi rend="italic">an gylde</hi> ‘for compensation’; nor yet ‘for a requital’, after <hi rend="italic">mercedem pro custodia consecutus</hi> (Lex Baiuw. XV 1). My transl. combines the ‘with, under’ taken from the instrumental and the negation into ‘only without’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_19-3.attnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope></bibl><label>onfó</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">underfo</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_19-3.attnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope></bibl><label>onfenge</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">underfenge</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_19-3.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Lit. ‘they shall both give it back in such condition as either of them has received it in.’ The object of this cap. according to Pollock and Maitland (<hi rend="italic">History of English Law</hi>, <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>. p. 31) was to prevent men, intent on homicide, from obtaining another man’s weapons and so obscuring incriminating evidence or permitting the homicide to swear an oath that it was with no weapon of his that the dead man was slain.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Af_19-3.whinote.n.2" n="2" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">413</biblScope></bibl><label>unstained</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Without it having been used to commit a crime.</seg></note>
      </div>
